  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate at 45-degree incidence. Initialize layer thicknesses using physics-informed lambda/(4n) scaling: for TiO2 layers use n~2.47, for SiO2 layers use n~1.46, with design wavelengths centered at 550nm (visible band center) and 850nm (NIR band center). Set minimum thickness bound to 35nm (relaxed from 30nm), maximum bound to 200nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with soft objectives: maximize reflectance in 450-650nm band, maximize transmittance in 700-1000nm band, minimize crosstalk (suppress transmittance in 450-650nm and reflectance in 700-1000nm). Evaluate unpolarized or both s- and p-polarization states. Output best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and final thicknesses_nm array for all candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 450-650 nm, 700-1000 nm. soft objectives: high reflectance in 450-650 nm; high transmittance in 700-1000 nm; minimized crosstalk between bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 450-650 nm; reflectance in 700-1000 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 24 layers.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating TiO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on a fused-silica substrate at 45-degree incidence. Use physics-informed quarter-wave scaling for initialization, enforce 35–200 nm thickness bounds, and apply a gradient-based thickness optimizer. Softly maximize reflectance in 450–650 nm, maximize transmittance in 700–1000 nm, while minimizing transmitted light in 450–650 nm and reflected light in 700–1000 nm. Evaluate unpolarized illumination across the visible-to-NIR spectral range.",
